##########  2. GET /api/registrations (paging)  ##########

### Case 14/15 - Default list, newest first (expect 200)
GET {{host}}/api/registrations

### Case 16 - Second page, size 5 (expect 200)
GET {{host}}/api/registrations?page=2&pageSize=5

### Case 17 - Page past the end (expect 200, empty items)
GET {{host}}/api/registrations?page=999

### Case 18 - Invalid page (expect 400)
GET {{host}}/api/registrations?page=0

### Case 19 - Page size too large (expect 400)
GET {{host}}/api/registrations?pageSize=100

##########  3. GET /api/registrations (filters)  ##########

### Case 20 - Filter by type (expect 200)
GET {{host}}/api/registrations?type=VIP

### Case 21 - Filter by status (expect 200)
GET {{host}}/api/registrations?status=Confirmed

### Case 22 - Filter by participant name (expect 200)
GET {{host}}/api/registrations?participantName=juan

### Case 23 - Name search ignores case (expect 200)
GET {{host}}/api/registrations?participantName=JUAN

### Case 24 - Partial name match (expect 200)
GET {{host}}/api/registrations?participantName=dela

### Case 25 - Combined filters (expect 200)
GET {{host}}/api/registrations?type=Competitor&status=Pending&participantName=juan

### Case 26 - No matches (expect 200, empty items)
GET {{host}}/api/registrations?participantName=zzzzzz

### Case 27 - Invalid type (expect 400)
GET {{host}}/api/registrations?type=Sponsor

### Case 28 - Invalid status (expect 400)
GET {{host}}/api/registrations?status=Done

##########  4. GET /api/registrations/{id}  ##########

### Case 29 - Existing ID, taken from Case 01 (expect 200)
GET {{host}}/api/registrations/{{case01.response.body.$.id}}

### Case 30 - ID that does not exist (expect 404)
GET {{host}}/api/registrations/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### Case 31 - Not a valid GUID (expect 404, no 500)
GET {{host}}/api/registrations/abc

##########  5. GET /api/registrations/summary  ##########

### Case 32-36, 38 - Summary (expect 200)
GET {{host}}/api/registrations/summary

### Case 37 - Summary updates after a new registration
# Step 1: run the summary above and note the numbers. Step 2: run this POST. Step 3: run the summary again.
# @name case37
POST {{host}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1037",
  "registrationType": "Exhibitor",
  "amountPaid": 500
}

### Case 37 - Step 3: summary again
GET {{host}}/api/registrations/summary

##########  6. Database persistence (manual)  ##########
### Case 39 - Restart the API, then run Case 14 and Case 29 again: same totalCount, Case 01 still found.
### Case 40 - Open carshow.db in DB Browser for SQLite: unique indexes on PlateNumber and RegistrationNumber.
